e deployment. The \"liability chill\" decried by accelerationists actually functions as a vital precautionary pause, preventing the release of capabilities that outpace our ability to ensure alignment. This position assumes that the threat of existential financial ruin is the primary mechanism capable of overcoming corporate deployment incentives. If developers prioritize reputational damage over financial risk, strict liability might play a smaller role in securing alignment. However, until developers can empirically prove their systems fail safely at scale, we must maintain the threat of uncapped liability to guarantee that progress remains strictly conditional on verifiable safeguards.",
