den of proof rests on those defending the status quo to justify the ongoing casualties of delayed innovation. Every year we delay, human drivers kill 40,000 Americans on the road, and human medical errors kill hundreds of thousands more in hospitals. Subjecting developers to an uncoordinated patchwork of state-level lawsuits paralyzes deployment, ensuring these preventable deaths continue. A predictable federal framework provides the market stability necessary to deploy autonomous systems that are statistically vastly superior to humans right now. We cannot allow the pursuit of legal perfection to perpetuate the daily tragedy of human error.",
