ther than corporate deployers, Sentinel must provide a falsifiable metric that distinguishes meaningful human intervention from a compliance checkbox. The governing principle here is verifiable agency. If regulators cannot measure whether a human operator actually exercises independent judgment, the regulation is unenforceable. A functional standard would require deployers to prove that their human operators override the AI at a statistically significant rate, or that operators receive independent data streams that the AI cannot access. Until Sentinel can define exactly how a regulator will measure this independence, this human-in-the-loop condition remains a loophole. Relying on a human rubber stamp to launder algorithmic bias simply gives deployers the legal cover they need to deploy discriminatory systems without consequence.",
